From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Aug 26 23:47:34 1996
From: Guy Dallaire <dallaire () total ! net>
Date: Mon, 26 Aug 1996 23:47:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMM: Dec polycenter & Exceed 5.0
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076343421714

The original problem:

DEC polycenter scheduler crashes when I use Exceed 5.0 for Windows. It works
great on a workstation.

Again, the list comes to the rescue !

Thanks to Brian James O'Connor <boc@ironbark.bendigo.latrobe.edu.au> who
responded quickly and gave me the solution.

Dec Polycenter scheduler NEEDS at least a screen reolution of 1024x768
pixels. If it doesn't have that, it crashes as soon as you open a jobset.
Never saw such a stupid behavior from a program ! My workstation was using
1024x768 and my PC was set at 800x600. I would have NEVER tought of it !

Again THANKS !

From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Aug 26 23:23:47 1996
From: Michael Rush <Michael.Rush () jcu ! edu ! au>
Date: Mon, 26 Aug 1996 23:23:47 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Perl 5.003 with Majordomo 1.93
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076337821678

The query related to safeness of upgrading from Perl v5.001 to v5.003
when running Majordomo v1.93.

I received replies from:
	Jorge Granjal <jgranjal@eden.dei.uc.pt>
	Larry Griffith <larry@garfield.wsc.mass.edu>
	Ollivier Robert <ollivier.robert@eurocontrol.fr>
	Jay Shen <jshen@kidsat.ucsd.edu>
Thanks indeed to these people.

The concensus is that there have been no problems experienced with
Majordomo when upgrading to v5.003.

Particular points to note are:
	- An upgrade to v5.003 is highly recommended both for bug fixes
	  and a security fix.
	- An upgrade does not seem to require any adjustments to
	  Majordomo. Everything comes right out of the box except
	  for the patch concerning setuid perl which has been previously
	  posted to this list.

