Original text follows:

We upgraded as per subject via 3.2 so it was two updates.  The process 
went smoothly after deleting the Decnet subsets which we don't use in the 
internet environment.   However there are a number of problems - some 
major, some minor.  I would appreciate any guidance.

1 All previously hosted domains outside our own (mcb.net) such as 
iomad.com which were CNAME records in hosts.db have disappeared.  This is 
very embarrassing.  Named is still the July 1995 version so update has 
not changed the name server but the daemon log in syslog.dated has 
numerous entries complaining that eg iomad.com is outside domain mcb.net 
...ignored.   If it worked as a simple CNAME pointer to our hostname 
(mannet) before what has 3.2c done that stops it now and how do we map in 
hosts.db so that registered domain names like iomad.com point to us?

2 DECTERM from the apllications menu does not start. The console log says 
it is starting but that is the last reference and no window appears and 
there is no error message on the console log.

3 tsch is the shell we have always used, but the capability to hihlight 
text with the mouse and the click the righjt mouse button to replicate 
the text (ie a mouse copy and paste) is lost.


There are other problems which I might refer to the list but I do not 
want to take advantage of everybody's goodwill.
Stuart McKenzie


THere were no solutions offered from the list but I am pleased to advise 
that we solved point one ourselves.   Under 3.0b you could get away with 
CNAME records to effectively alias other domains to your own.  In 3.2c 
you cannot.  It is necessary to create host files, pointed to by your 
primary boot file (named.boot) which have proper SOA records and CNAMEs 
of their own for www or whatever.   So far we have been unable to tweak 
either dns or sendmail to have mail addressed to iomad.com be redirected 
to iomad.mcb.net which has its own ip address.  The MX record in the new 
host file is
iomad.com.	IN	MX	0	iomad.mcb.net.

but mail sent to postmaster@iomad.com disappears into the ether!!

The other points remain unresolved at present although DEC support said 
that DECTERM should work - they then tried it on their machine and it 
didn't!  It seems to be a configuration parameter that has changed.

Stuart McKenzie

