Hello managers,

Sometimes our DEC Alpha 2100 has a panic error event. The situation is
always the same:

While the machine is making a backup copy of the all AdvFS filesets
(vdump using clone filesets), it (the machine) shutdown and comes up
againg working fine.

We make a level 0 vdump once per week, and an incremental vdump the
other days without problems but, once per 4 or 5 months the machine
crash.

The uerf command gives the following information:

>********************************* ENTRY     2. *********************************
>
>----- EVENT INFORMATION -----
>
>EVENT CLASS                             ERROR EVENT
>OS EVENT TYPE                  302.     PANIC
>SEQUENCE NUMBER                  3.
>OPERATING SYSTEM                        DEC OSF/1
>OCCURRED/LOGGED ON                      Wed Aug 14 08:34:16 1996
>OCCURRED ON SYSTEM                      airas
>SYSTEM ID                 x00020009     CPU TYPE:  DEC 2100
>SYSTYPE                   x00000000
>MESSAGE                                 panic (cpu 0): N1 = -1027

In the /var/adm/crash directory saves de audit-data.0, bounds,
crash-data.0, vmcore.0 and vmunix.0 files. I include the crash-data.0
file in the attachment.

The questions are: Has anybody the same problem?, Any ideas about the
problem?

Thank you very much in advance.
 
-- 
J. Carlos Sanchez Rivas <csanchez@cirp.es>
Responsable de Sistemas Hardware
Centro de I.L.L. Ramon Pi~neiro, GALICIA (SPAIN)

