Thanks to the following for their responses:

cherkus@UniMaster.COM
theissen@pfh.research.philips.com
Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com
rjackson@portal.gmu.edu

I first asked which O/S should I use since I got the DU 4.0 upgrade before
the 3.2G arrived, with a newer version of the firmware.  It seems that the
v3.2G is supposed to support recently released hardware that DU 4.0 does
not yet support.  Interesting set of circumstances.

Then the firmware that I need to install on my AS 250-4/266 appears to be
the same as that for the AS 200 systems, which is distinct from the AS 255
systems.  This was sort of implied in the docs on the CD rom.

And about the auto-port selection of the ethernet, if it doesn't find
any signals on the TP port, it defaults to the AUI, even though the
console environment says to go TP.  More than one person has seen this
on their systems.

eyc

